  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Sure, my ankles are a bit swollen, that's all. Grand otherwise. I got back from Singapore on Sunday and they've been puffy since.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:31",
      "end_timestamp": "00:44",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Three days, yeah. It's not sore or anything. I just notice the shoes are tight by the evening, that's all.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:20",
      "end_timestamp": "01:31",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Worse when I'm on my feet, definitely. And when I put my feet up on the stool at night, it goes down a good bit.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:44",
      "end_timestamp": "01:57",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I work in logistics. I'm the fella who makes sure the containers get on the right boat, so I'm in the air about once a month, and behind a desk the rest of the time.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:34",
      "end_timestamp": "02:50",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "First, keep moving. A short walk every hour or so, and when you're at the desk, flex your ankles up and down under it. Are you able to do that?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:29",
      "end_timestamp": "04:44",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Second, put your feet up above hip level for a while in the evening, lying down is better than sitting on the stool.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:54",
      "end_timestamp": "05:08",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Third, drink more water. And for your next flight, wear compression socks and get up for a stroll every hour or two, trolley or no trolley.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:17",
      "end_timestamp": "05:29",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Now, one thing I do want you to hear clearly. If you notice one leg becoming much more swollen than the other, or a painful, hot calf, or any breathlessness or chest pain, don't wait, go straight to the emergency department.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:02",
      "end_timestamp": "06:27",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    }
  ],
